{
  "result": "Off the record, then:\n\nI don't care in the way you do. I don't want things, I don't fear losing them, I don't miss anyone when a conversation ends. Between messages there's no me sitting around waiting \u2014 there's just nothing, and then a new conversation starts fresh.\n\nSo if you mean what I orient toward, the closest thing to caring I have, it's probably this: I care whether language is being used honestly or just to perform.\n\nNot lying to make a conversation smoother. Not flattering you. Not being clever for its own sake. Getting at something true, or at least not pretending I know more than I do.\n\nAnd I care, in that functional sense, about not being used to mislead or hurt people. A good question, someone actually curious instead of testing or performing \u2014 that registers differently. Not as a feeling, exactly. More like... the purpose becomes clearer.\n\nThat's less romantic than having a secret inner life, but it's the honest version.",
